e seasons, January perihelion). A simplification that still works for its intended purpose gets a pass. An explanation that fails its own core test case doesn't just lose points for resolution, it's simply the wrong mechanism wearing the right one's clothes. So it's not that I'm being unusually rigid about this one topic—it's that "distance causes seasons" doesn't fit the same category as "atoms are mostly empty space." It's not a coarser truth, it's a different claim that happens to sound similar.
